TI  - Making Common Fund data more findable: catalyzing a data ecosystem.
LID - 10.1093/gigascience/giac105 [doi]
LID - giac105
AB  - The Common Fund Data Ecosystem (CFDE) has created a flexible system of data 
      federation that enables researchers to discover datasets from across the US 
      National Institutes of Health Common Fund without requiring that data owners 
      move, reformat, or rehost those data. This system is centered on a catalog that 
      integrates detailed descriptions of biomedical datasets from individual Common 
      Fund Programs' Data Coordination Centers (DCCs) into a uniform metadata model 
      that can then be indexed and searched from a centralized portal. This Crosscut 
      Metadata Model (C2M2) supports the wide variety of data types and metadata terms 
      used by individual DCCs and can readily describe nearly all forms of biomedical 
      research data. We detail its use to ingest and index data from 11 DCCs.
